{"id":"rel.wave2.batch04.local-ring-unique-maximal.to.two-sided-ideal","from_formulation":"form.4f7edb6d32334f67.local-ring-unique-maximal","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.two-sided-ideal","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"maximal ideal","editorial_reason":"Unique maximality is a property of ideals of a commutative ring; an ordinary ideal provides the necessary underlying structure but not the maximality criterion.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07BH","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AIdeal_of_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_scope_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch04.jacobson-radical-ring.to.two-sided-ideal","from_formulation":"form.90b0d1ecfa394230.jacobson-radical-ring","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.two-sided-ideal","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"maximal ideals","editorial_reason":"A Jacobson radical is an intersection of maximal ideals. General ring ideals are a genuine prerequisite; maximality and the intersection construction remain separate.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AMD","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AIdeal_of_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_scope_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch04.annihilator-module.to.two-sided-ideal","from_formulation":"form.a9ca2e716ceffd36.annihilator-module","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.two-sided-ideal","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"the ideal","editorial_reason":"The module annihilator is explicitly an ideal of the scalar ring; it requires the additive subgroup and two-sided absorption axioms before imposing the annihilation condition.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080S","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AIdeal_of_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_scope_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch04.annihilator-module.to.left-module-nonunital","from_formulation":"form.a9ca2e716ceffd36.annihilator-module","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.left-module-nonunital","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"R-module M","editorial_reason":"The annihilator of M is defined using an R-module scalar action. The screened left-module definition gives the underlying action without erasing any source-specific unitality requirement.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080S","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AModule_over_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_scope_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
